      "message": "* **Magic Numbers:** `fun.c` relies heavily on raw hex bytes in the arrays (e.g., `write_bin_cmd[] \u003d { 0xdc, 0, 0, 0 ... 0x03, 0, 0 };`). While common in low-level SCSI/USB work, extracting these command opcodes (e.g., `0xdc`, `0x03`) into `#define` macros or `enums` in `ff_sg_io.h` will make the command construction highly readable.",
